@HELP: Input Queue Panel -- Fields              !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
{  JOBNAME  }The name of the job, started task or TSO user.
{  TYPE     }JOB, STC or TSU.
{  JNUM     }The JES2 job number.
{  PRTY     }The JES2 priority, 0 to 15. Can be overtyped.
{  C        }The job class; $ for a TSO user, # for a started task. Can
}            be overtyped.
{  POS      }The place of a waiting job among the jobs of its class.
{  DEST     }Where the output goes: LOCAL, or Rn. Can be overtyped.
{  RMT      }Not filled yet.
{  NODE     }The JES2 node, 1.
{  SAFF     }The system the job is bound to, if it is bound to one.
{  ASYS     }The system the job is active on.
{  STAT     }HOLD if the job is held.
}
}  The ? command, typed alone, shows the further fields of the jobs as
}  on the Status panel: the programmer's name, the account, NOTIFY, the
}  times the job was read in and started, and more (Status panel help,
}  topic 4). PF11 and PF10 move them; ? again goes back.
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Input Queue help   PF3: back to SDSF
